course: dictionary
lesson: 6814
title: Words about teeth and braces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An orthodontist is a kind of dentist. Read the words around it for clues: «Braces slowly move teeth with steady pressure over months or years, and an orthodontist usually decides on them around age 12 or older.» Braces and moving teeth are the clues, so an orthodontist is a person who works on braces and teeth.
explain: Break the word into parts for more clues. Ortho is a Greek word meaning straight, and odont means tooth. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it: "an orthodontist usually decides on them" still makes sense if an orthodontist is a teeth specialist who straightens teeth.
explain: Not every tooth helper is an orthodontist. A dentist looks after teeth in general, but an orthodontist specialises in straightening teeth and fixing how teeth and jaws fit together. Specialise means to focus on one particular area of work.
explain: The sentence also gives a reason: «they are not only for looks, because straighter teeth can bite better and are easier to clean.» So straight teeth help you bite and keep clean, not just look nice.
fact: An orthodontist is a dentist who specialises in straightening teeth.
fact: Orthodontists fix the way teeth and jaws fit together, often by fitting braces.
fact: Many children see an orthodontist at about 10 to 14 years old.
fact: Braces move teeth slowly, with steady pressure over months or years.
fact: Ortho comes from a Greek word meaning straight, and odont means tooth.
exercise: «Braces slowly move teeth with steady pressure over months or years.» Which helper often fits braces? | *An orthodontist | A plumber | A baker | A pilot
exercise: What does the word orthodontist mean? | A person who sells toothbrushes | A teacher of maths | *A dentist who straightens teeth and fixes how teeth and jaws fit together | A doctor who treats broken bones
exercise: «They are not only for looks, because straighter teeth can bite better and are easier to clean.» Why are straighter teeth useful? | They stop you ever needing a dentist | *They can bite better and are easier to clean | They only look nicer | They make you taller
test: Your friend says an orthodontist pulls out teeth for fun. What is wrong with that idea? | An orthodontist only paints teeth | An orthodontist works on cars | *An orthodontist straightens teeth and fixes how teeth and jaws fit, often with braces | An orthodontist pulls out teeth for fun
test: In «an orthodontist usually decides on them around age 12 or older», what does them most likely mean? | Dinners | *Braces | Holidays | Birthdays
exam: In the sentence about braces, which clue best helps you work out the meaning of orthodontist? | The word months | Age alone | *Braces and moving teeth with steady pressure | The word usually
